<mxfile host="Electron" agent="Codex drawio-skill">
  <diagram id="ai-research-conceptual-erd" name="Conceptual ERD" data-source="popper/docs/architecture.md §1, §4, §6, §7; subsystems/state.md §1, §2; subsystems/research-program.md §1–§2; subsystems/error-control.md §2; subsystems/stage-1…stage-5 (stage-2 §2 data acquisition); subsystems/runtime.md §7–§10; subsystems/views-and-visualization.md §1; subsystems/evaluation.md §5" data-model="Conceptual level: entity names, relationships and crow&#39;s-foot cardinality only. Lines that cross the dashed Popper boundary are the platform↔Popper interface (architecture §4). Platform entities cover the responsibilities architecture §1 leaves to the calling platform (authentication, organizations and projects, billing, notifications, collaboration, publication workflow, dataset ingestion); runs and artifacts are tenant-scoped (§7). PolicyVersion, DecisionRequest, UsageRecord, EvaluationDecision and DatasetAssessment are Popper records surfaced through the Settings API, human decision points, resource reporting, evaluation and data acquisition (architecture §7.1, runtime §7/§10, evaluation §5, stage-2 §2); the platform ingests and versions an approved snapshot. Every work product is an immutable Artifact with one envelope (state §1.4), so Artifact is not a separate box. Events, traces, Construct, DataLead, Critique, Theory, Campaign, MethodLesson and Statement belong to the logical ERDs.">
